---
import ListItem from "../components/ListItem.astro";
import Panel from "../components/Panel.astro";
---

<Panel>
    <h1>Infrastructure Setup Skills</h1>
    <p>4+ years professional experience. Click each for more details.</p>
    <ListItem
        title="Kubernetes"
        >I took the initiative to refactor our Kubernetes manifest setup to be
        4x more DRY, using a small shell script to generate per-environment
        (dev/cert/preprod/prod) versions of our 40+ deployments, jobs, and Nginx
        ingresses/Istio httproutes. My script uses <a
            href="https://github.com/mikefarah/yq">yq</a
        > to easily propagate global, per-environment, and per-deployment environment
        variables.</ListItem
    >
    <ListItem title="Google Cloud Platform/GCP"
        >Created the CI/CD infrastructure (including deploy keys) to manage GCP
        deployments and secrets. Experienced with production support (using K8S
        CLI and <a href="https://github.com/sarub0b0/kubetui">TUIs</a>) to the
        extent that I mentored newer engineers on how to more efficiently
        monitor and modify deployments.</ListItem
    >
    <ListItem title="GitLab CI/CD">
        Upgraded our CI/CD infrastructure to use GitLab for both image storage
        and CI/CD (including creating the <a
            href="https://chromewebstore.google.com/detail/deployment-environments-f/ihenkkccaaacabdgcendjljnoolncbbg?authuser=1&hl=en"
            >Deployment Environments for GitLab</a
        > browser extension to improve the UX), eliminating the need for semi-manual
        deployments.
    </ListItem>
    <ListItem title="Docker and Docker Compose"
        >Lead the simplification of our Docker setup, using newer Docker
        multi-image Dockerfile features to drop the Dockerfile count in our main
        repo from 3 to 1, greatly improving ease of comprehension and
        maintenance. Took initiative to leverage YAML anchors to eliminate
        environment variable duplication for our 33 Docker Compose services.
    </ListItem>
</Panel>
